Z||000001||Oreif||08-08-2000||02:25 PM||||I read thru it and most of it is common sense stuff. The only thing I'd like to add would be on tinted windows. I have a friend who is a police officer and as for tinted windows, most officers hate them because they cannot see in the car. Especially at night. He says the best way to make a good impression on the officer "before" he gets to your dark tinted car at night is to turn on your interior lights. He will be able to see in the car and that may give you some extra points and he may let you off with a warning. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||08-08-2000||07:14 PM||||On the advise to not admit guilt... 'I had no idea I was _____ '. <P>I have had a couple of police friends over the years tell me that would make them MORE likely to ticket someone in this situation. The theory being that they are not paying attention and probably more dangerous than someone intentionally driving say 10 over...<P>Also, tell the truth (or a REALLY good lie)... An obvious lie will get you a ticket faster than just about anything...||||reg||1
